= Introduction <chap-introduction>

This chapter sets out the question the book answers and why it matters. It also explains how the rest of the book is organized, so a reader can choose where to start.

== Motivation <sec-motivation>

Measuring uncertainty well is older than most of the methods used to do it. The foundations of information theory @shannon1948 still shape how we reason about noise and signal, and resampling @efron1979 made it practical to attach error bars to estimates that have no tidy formula.#footnote[Footnotes suit short asides that would interrupt the main argument.]

== Outline <sec-outline>

#ref(<chap-methods>, supplement: [Chapter]) describes the approach and the estimators it compares. #ref(<chap-results>, supplement: [Chapter]) reports what happens when those estimators are run on simulated data. The appendix collects a derivation that the main text only sketches.
